1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:01,480
Mr.

2
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:03,220
Tommy

3
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:26,780
Once or no, I can't wait, perlu, limited to the self-size

4
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:56,760
See you next time.

5
00:00:56,780 --> 00:01:26,760
See you next time.

6
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:28,780
See you next time.

7
00:01:56,780 --> 00:01:58,580
And you're also being rude.

8
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:01,280
Sorry, it's long!

9
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:05,760
Damn it.

10
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,680
Just five more centimeters.

11
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,020
You can reach that.

12
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:10,520
Jump higher.

13
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:11,360
Reach it.

14
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:25,840
Off his foot!

15
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:29,620
Shuyo Hidaka demonstrates formidable balance and skill.

16
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:33,960
Karasuno narrowly manages to stop Inazaki from scoring a breakpoint.

17
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:35,600
Damn it.

18
00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:37,580
Don't get exhausted now.

19
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,220
Complaint, dumbass!

20
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:45,820
Complaint about what?

21
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:48,940
Give me one more!

22
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:58,380
I honestly thought nothing really scared Kageyama anymore.

23
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:04,560
But it's not only the people across enemy lines that can push you all the way to your limit.

24
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:11,680
I'm impressed, Hinata.

25
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:20,320
And Inazaki quickly takes back possession of service.

26
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:24,260
I'm astounded that they have the guts to go straight from the middle whenever they're in trouble.

27
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,120
And that goes for both teams.

28
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:30,500
There are times when Natsuma's concentration just sort of snaps suddenly.

29
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:36,360
But today, for some reason, it actually feels like it keeps getting sharper and sharper.

30
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:41,340
But I do think there are some actual monsters out there.

31
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:43,880
Yeah, I'd agree there are at least a few real ones.

32
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:48,760
True monsters who love playing volleyball day in and day out.

33
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:53,320
And I get to meet them, stand on the same court with them, to face them head on.

34
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,720
Look at me.

35
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:58,460
I'm a human being with an invitation to go to the Monster's Ball.

36
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:00,720
I'm a lucky guy.

37
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:11,460
The only way to go forward is through this team!

38
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:12,320
Yeah!

39
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:16,680
Atsumumiya is serving.

40
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:21,120
He'd been amusing himself by battling it out with Nishinoya.

41
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:24,740
But there's no telling who he'll bear his fangs at next.

42
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:30,300
I can't even imagine the pressure the Karasuno receivers are feeling right now.

43
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:50,060
Right on the heels of Karasuno's Kageyama, Inanazaki's Atsumumiya pulls off an ace of his own.

44
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:54,740
An exchange of high-level serves that makes it hard to believe this is a high school game.

45
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:58,420
It's an unending cycle of hope followed by despair.

46
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,160
Dude.

47
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,620
The ball's in your face before you even know it!

48
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:07,680
And once again, Inanazaki is at match point.

49
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:14,600
Guys, we don't need any miracles.

50
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:17,860
Go, go, let's go, Inanai!

51
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:20,420
Go, go, let's go, Inanai!

52
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,660
This is how all of our matches go!

53
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:23,820
Inanai!

54
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,780
Go, go, let's go, Inanai!

55
00:05:25,780 --> 00:05:28,400
Karasuno's down match point and they're still not scared?

56
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:31,860
I mean, Atsumumiya's serving and they're hanging on by the skin of their teeth.

57
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,000
Let's go, Inanai!

58
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:37,080
If they push us one step back, we'll go over the edge.

59
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:39,920
I will never get used to this.

60
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:42,580
I think my hands and knees are shaking.

61
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:45,480
But we're not looking for a miracle here.

62
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:51,100
We're going to do what we've done time and time again and we'll survive like we always do.

63
00:05:51,100 --> 00:06:10,840
A roar out of the silence!

64
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:16,760
After that graceful jump flow serve, he shakes up Karasuno with an intense spike serve!

65
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:18,160
It's going over the net!

66
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:27,140
I'm not going to lose!

67
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,420
I'm not going to lose!

68
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:31,580
Give me one more!

69
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:39,260
I refuse to lose to him!

70
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,020
This is bad.

71
00:06:45,220 --> 00:06:47,560
Shouyo Hirata runs right down the center!

72
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:51,940
The ball was about to go over the net, but Tobio Kageyama sets it even higher!

73
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:53,380
Hidey-ho!

74
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:54,860
That was up there!

75
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:57,200
It's like young Hinata has wings!

76
00:06:57,520 --> 00:07:00,520
And the set, I can't believe the ball got to him!

77
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:00,720
Ha!

78
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:01,520
Hmm?

79
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:02,440
What's up?

80
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:05,060
It's not because he believes in the setter.

81
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:05,460
Thank you!

82
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:06,540
Great job, Hinata!

83
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:07,340
He just knows.

84
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:09,820
He knows that the ball will come to it.

85
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:10,860
I thought they had a good chance!

86
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,600
He just assumes they'll get him the ball!

87
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:17,440
You have my condolences, Kageyama.

88
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:21,240
That is one terrifying partner you've got there.

89
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:23,820
And what's so weird about that?

90
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:31,440
Hala, you need to stop and think some more about other people's feelings!

91
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:32,040
Huh.

92
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,400
That's funny.

93
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,800
From a heartless bastard like you.

94
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:36,120
I was not making a joke!

95
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:39,880
Huh?

96
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:42,460
I win.

97
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,400
Hey, what?

98
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,080
Stop looking at me like that!

99
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,460
I'm the one who scored the point!

100
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:47,360
What's your deal?

101
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:49,400
It's thanks to me you got that.

102
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:50,520
Nice kill.

103
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:53,400
Don't say it with that look on your face!

104
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:55,320
Make it count!

105
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,360
Good, good, good!

106
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:59,380
Their number 10 is finally in the back row!

107
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:02,340
Two more rotations until Asahi serves.

108
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,780
That's probably going to be our best bet.

109
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:07,320
Don't let them get any break points before then!

110
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:09,380
Man, I'm tired.

111
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:11,420
Tired of running at full speed.

112
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:12,780
Tired of jumping.

113
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,480
Tired of their stupid, unpredictable setter.

114
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:19,840
Samu, front!

115
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:32,320
If I could just stuff him right now and end it, I'm sure the whole team would lose their minds.

116
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:35,260
But, I can't do that.

117
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:40,320
So, you better be there.

118
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:47,740
Oh, middle blocker Hidata gets the ball back in the air!

119
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,640
Excellent positioning, I'd say.

120
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:51,760
Go, Hidata!

121
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:54,420
Ah, dang it.

122
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:57,440
I thought I already knew this, but...

123
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:58,240
Wow.

124
00:08:59,020 --> 00:09:01,200
He is an incredible blocker!

125
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:07,540
Please, God, or Buddha, or Goddess, or...

126
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:08,200
Or whatever!

127
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:10,880
Just please, let us have this one point.

128
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:12,640
Counter!

129
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:16,220
Back minus!

130
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,000
Nice receive!

131
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,140
Holy cow!

132
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:28,600
How did he manage to get anywhere close to that?

133
00:09:29,060 --> 00:09:31,700
That play, that guy, is so amazing!

134
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,300
The receive was awesome, sure.

135
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:37,560
But he was able to get that ball because he's working with the blockers.

136
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:42,340
All the spikers on the court want to beat out every block and every reception.

137
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:46,140
The setters want to give the spiker the best advantage possible.

138
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:50,380
The servers want to attack hard enough that the setter doesn't have to do anything.

139
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:53,520
They all work together until the ball hits the ground.

140
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:57,460
If you lose your train of thought for even a second, you get left behind.

141
00:09:59,140 --> 00:09:59,860
Damn it!

142
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:03,220
My mind is clear, but my legs can't keep up.

143
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:13,880
Shit, sorry.

144
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,580
Karasuno can barely keep standing.

145
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:19,020
Kageyama!

146
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:22,660
You've got this.

147
00:10:23,140 --> 00:10:24,020
You've got this.

148
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:26,340
Asahi!

149
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:26,980
Now!

150
00:10:30,140 --> 00:10:31,140
It's perfect.

151
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:35,260
The first and second years will get to keep hitting these sets.

152
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:37,960
And so will the new players.

153
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:39,840
I'm kind of jealous.

154
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,400
Three blockers!

155
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,880
But I also feel a little sorry for them.

156
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:50,760
Damn it.

157
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:06,040
Quick, quick, you're Capacito!

158
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:08,640
Heck yeah!

159
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:10,360
Nice kill!

160
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:14,860
That pisses me off.

161
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:15,700
Wait, what?

162
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:16,620
What does?

163
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:19,160
You see him shift the timing on that spike?

164
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:22,560
He was experimenting with that at our practice match, remember?

165
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:24,120
Wait, he was?

166
00:11:24,580 --> 00:11:27,480
He waits for the blockers to start falling before he hits.

167
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:31,440
If he messes that up, it would end up being a weak-ass spike.

168
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:32,920
I've never noticed that before.

169
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:36,820
He probably hasn't even mastered it yet, but he made it work there.

170
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:42,080
And towards the end of the game, when everyone is exhausted, somehow he maintains perfect form in the air.

171
00:11:42,860 --> 00:11:44,460
Man, that guy pissed me off.

172
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:49,300
And now it's Karasuno's turn to try and end this game!

173
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:53,060
I think I'm starting to get chest pains from all this stress.

174
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:54,540
Hmm.

175
00:11:54,540 --> 00:12:00,040
So, the guys out on the court, how do you think they're feeling right about now?

176
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:00,700
Ugh.

177
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:03,540
Well, I bet they're all just running on fumes at this point.

178
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:07,120
And they're also probably fighting off a serious amount of pressure and nervous jitters.

179
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:08,600
Hmph.

180
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:15,200
They're also thinking, whoever scores here will be a hero.

181
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:32,500
Just one more point.

182
00:12:33,220 --> 00:12:34,060
Come on.

183
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Come on!

184
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:47,720
Does he have to get so giddy over every single thing these first years do?

185
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:50,780
Number one high school setter, my ass.

186
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:57,320
Man, I'm so spoiled.

187
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:00,720
The pressure of the guy demanding the ball?

188
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:04,140
The murderous rage of a guy who's determined to kill the ball?

189
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:05,820
It's the best!

190
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:13,260
And I get to use it all as a decoy.

191
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,600
It doesn't get any better than that.

192
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,860
I'm not gonna let them stop me here.

193
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:25,740
They don't get to push back my attacks.

194
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:28,980
They're my attacks, but okay, sure.

195
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:30,000
Let's put it away.

196
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:31,920
And Tsuna makes the point.

197
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:35,800
And Narazaki's attackers have Karasuno's defense at their mercy field.

198
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:40,600
The Mia twins haven't actually landed their quicks very often during the match we've seen today.

199
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:44,060
But they still have an impact whenever they fake them effectively.

200
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:49,420
I'm fairly certain Natsuma was quite eager to keep playing with the new toy he's found.

201
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:52,100
But he's showing some nice restraint.

202
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:56,300
I hear the game on court A is intense.

203
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:58,780
It's the last set and they might hit 30.

204
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,180
30 points?

205
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:01,160
I would die.

206
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:05,900
And Narazaki gets this one up too!

207
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:07,040
Sabu!

208
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:09,300
Their blockers are stubbornly persistent.

209
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:13,520
Their nerves must be so frayed that the smallest thing can cause them to snap.

210
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,600
But they are not going to let that happen.

211
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:18,820
The concentration on both sides is simply tremendous.

212
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:23,400
Look at that high spike from Ananogiro.

213
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:25,680
Yeah!

214
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:28,720
And the crowd goes wild!

215
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:32,000
That spike went right over the block!

216
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:36,360
And Narazaki has grabbed Karasuno's tail and they refuse to let go.

217
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:39,360
Osamumi is in the back, so there won't be a quick.

218
00:14:39,660 --> 00:14:41,240
We've got to use this chance to score.

219
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:48,980
It's long!

220
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:51,040
It's long!

221
00:14:51,940 --> 00:14:55,380
But that punk's going to get the ball in the air.

222
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,400
Gotcha!

223
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:05,720
I do not believe it!

224
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:09,060
The audacity of first-year Tobio Kageyama!

225
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:12,700
Hmm.

226
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:19,520
Seems as though every Karasano player has been on the offense of this entire game!

227
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:28,520
They are certainly very focused on the attack, and while that is the source of Karasano's strength, I imagine it consumes a lot of physical and mental energy.

228
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:33,520
One more point...

229
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:36,520
Just one more...

230
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:50,520
It's not gonna make it!

231
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:51,520
Up front!

232
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:57,520
Son of a bitch! He's been going for that soft serve the whole time!

233
00:15:58,520 --> 00:15:59,520
It's you!

234
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:01,520
Back, back!

235
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:05,520
Chance ball!

236
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:09,520
Attack!

237
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:11,520
Attack!

238
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:12,520
Hurry!

239
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:14,520
We have to be faster than them!

240
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:16,520
Before the enemy gets back on their feet!

241
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:18,520
Before they catch up!

242
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:23,520
Wow, that was fast!

243
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:25,520
Karasano goes in for the kill!

244
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:27,520
But the leave it on Akagi saves it!

245
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:30,520
Slower guy, slow the game down!

246
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:32,520
Left enemy, slow it down!

247
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:38,520
A line shot!

248
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:39,520
Don't let it through!

249
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:42,520
Left!

250
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:45,520
Left!

251
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:48,520
They're already blocking!

252
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,520
My approach was too short!

253
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,520
I'll rebound it!

254
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:53,520
Come on! One more time!

255
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:55,520
Karasano!

256
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:58,520
Take it easy! Slow it down!

257
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:03,520
Their determination to score that point right this minute is speeding up their rhythm.

258
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:05,520
Speed can be a bad influence!

259
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:09,520
It narrows your view and shortens your breath!

260
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:16,520
It does make it harder for the other team, but at the same time, you're still struggling yourselves!

261
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:19,520
Back to the net! Now, do it!

262
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:20,520
That's mine!

263
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:21,520
That's mine!

264
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:22,520
That's mine!

265
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:23,520
That's mine!

